// The struct's `{` is never closed, so the parser gives up on the declaration
// and skips to the end of the file. Everything below is a run of source the
// tree does not account for: the import, the function, and the binding inside
// it. Nothing is reported about any of them, and nothing is reported about
// what they would have reached — that is the whole of what a half-read module
// costs, and it is the only thing it costs.

struct Route {

